{
  "mn127:0.1": "Middle Discourses 127 ",
  "mn127:0.2": "With Anuruddha ",
  "mn127:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn127:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn127:2.1": "And then the chamberlain Pañcakaṅga addressed a man, ",
  "mn127:2.2": "“Please, my man, go to Venerable Anuruddha, and in my name bow with your head to his feet. Say to him, ",
  "mn127:2.3": "‘Sir, the chamberlain Pañcakaṅga bows with his head to your feet.’ ",
  "mn127:2.4": "And then ask him whether he ",
  "mn127:2.5": "would please accept tomorrow’s meal from Pañcakaṅga together with the mendicant Saṅgha. ",
  "mn127:2.6": "And ask whether he might please come earlier than usual, ",
  "mn127:2.7": "for Pañcakaṅga has many duties, and much work to do for the king.” ",
  "mn127:2.8": "“Yes, sir,” that man replied. He did as Pañcakaṅga asked, and ",
  "mn127:2.9": "",
  "mn127:2.10": "",
  "mn127:2.11": "",
  "mn127:2.12": "",
  "mn127:2.13": "Venerable Anuruddha consented with silence. ",
  "mn127:3.1": "Then when the night had passed, Anuruddha robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, went to Pañcakaṅga’s home, where he sat down on the seat spread out. ",
  "mn127:3.2": "Then Pañcakaṅga served and satisfied Anuruddha with his own hands with delicious fresh and cooked foods. ",
  "mn127:3.3": "When Anuruddha had eaten and washed his hands and bowl, Pañcakaṅga took a low seat, sat to one side, ",
  "mn127: